IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgg-scope`
IMPORT `sgg-names`

-- Tests for sgg-names.l4 (s 378). Expected values are written from the text of each subsection, beside the assertion.
-- Dates: Date day month year. A `-- EXPECT` comment above a #TRACE says what the trace must print; the lead checks each against the output.

§ `Section 378(1): names the Registrar must refuse`

-- Arguments: the Minister has consented; subsection (2) provides the Registrar is not to refuse; the name is one under which the company is to carry on business in Singapore;
-- in the Registrar's opinion the name is (a) undesirable; (b) identical to another name; (c) identical to a reserved name; (d) a name or kind the Minister has directed the Registrar not to accept.
#ASSERT `s 378(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- none of the four opinions is held.
#ASSERT `s 378(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "Except with the consent of the Minister or as provided in subsection (2)".
#ASSERT `s 378(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 378(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a name under which the company is not to carry on business in Singapore is not one the subsection reaches.
#ASSERT `s 378(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 378(2): further names the Registrar must refuse`

-- the years that must have passed, paragraph by paragraph.
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the years that must have passed after the date of dissolution, cancellation or cessation` `s 378(2)(a)(i) a company dissolved following its winding up under Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the years that must have passed after the date of dissolution, cancellation or cessation` `s 378(2)(a)(ii) a company dissolved following its name being struck off the register under section 344 or 344A` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the years that must have passed after the date of dissolution, cancellation or cessation` `s 378(2)(b) a person whose registration and registration of the business name was cancelled under the Business Names Registration Act 2014 or had ceased under section 22 of that Act` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the years that must have passed after the date of dissolution, cancellation or cessation` `s 378(2)(c) a foreign company notice of the dissolution of which was given to the Registrar under section 377(2)` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the years that must have passed after the date of dissolution, cancellation or cessation` `s 378(2)(d)(i) a limited liability partnership dissolved following its winding up under section 39 of, and the Fifth Schedule to, the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the years that must have passed after the date of dissolution, cancellation or cessation` `s 378(2)(d)(ii) a limited liability partnership dissolved following its name being struck off the register kept under section 63 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the years that must have passed after the date of dissolution, cancellation or cessation` `s 378(2)(e)(i) a limited partnership whose registration was cancelled under section 14(1) or 19(4) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the years that must have passed after the date of dissolution, cancellation or cessation` `s 378(2)(e)(ii) a limited partnership dissolved, notice of which was lodged with the Registrar of Limited Partnerships under section 19(2) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the years that must have passed after the date of dissolution, cancellation or cessation` `s 378(2)(f)(i) a VCC dissolved following its winding up under Part 11 of the VCC Act` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the years that must have passed after the date of dissolution, cancellation or cessation` `s 378(2)(f)(ii) a VCC dissolved following its name being struck off the register under section 344 or 344A as applied by section 130B of the VCC Act` EQUALS 6

-- the arithmetic of "a period of at least N years has passed after the date": dissolved 1 June 2024, 2 years run to 1 June 2026.
#ASSERT `s 378 a period of at least the number of units has passed after the date` (Date 1 6 2024) (Date 2 6 2026) 2 Years EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378 a period of at least the number of units has passed after the date` (Date 1 6 2024) (Date 1 6 2026) 2 Years EQUALS FALSE

-- Arguments: the Minister has consented; the day of the registration; the name is identical to the name of the earlier holder; the earlier holder; the day of the dissolution, cancellation or cessation. Registration on 1 June 2026.
-- (a)(i) winding up, 2 years: dissolved 1 January 2025 runs to 1 January 2027, so the period has not passed; dissolved 1 January 2024 runs to 1 January 2026, so it has.
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(a)(i) a company dissolved following its winding up under Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(a)(i) a company dissolved following its winding up under Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` (Date 1 1 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the boundary: dissolved 1 June 2024, so the 2 years end on 1 June 2026 itself, and a registration on that day is not yet after the period.
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(a)(i) a company dissolved following its winding up under Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` (Date 1 6 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 2 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(a)(i) a company dissolved following its winding up under Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` (Date 1 6 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a)(ii) struck off, 6 years.
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(a)(ii) a company dissolved following its name being struck off the register under section 344 or 344A` (Date 1 1 2021) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(a)(ii) a company dissolved following its name being struck off the register under section 344 or 344A` (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) business name, one year.
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(b) a person whose registration and registration of the business name was cancelled under the Business Names Registration Act 2014 or had ceased under section 22 of that Act` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(b) a person whose registration and registration of the business name was cancelled under the Business Names Registration Act 2014 or had ceased under section 22 of that Act` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) foreign company dissolved, 2 years.
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(c) a foreign company notice of the dissolution of which was given to the Registrar under section 377(2)` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(c) a foreign company notice of the dissolution of which was given to the Registrar under section 377(2)` (Date 1 1 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (d) limited liability partnership: winding up 2 years, struck off 6 years.
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(d)(i) a limited liability partnership dissolved following its winding up under section 39 of, and the Fifth Schedule to, the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(d)(ii) a limited liability partnership dissolved following its name being struck off the register kept under section 63 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` (Date 1 1 2021) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(d)(ii) a limited liability partnership dissolved following its name being struck off the register kept under section 63 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (e) limited partnership: cancelled one year, dissolved one year.
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(e)(i) a limited partnership whose registration was cancelled under section 14(1) or 19(4) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(e)(ii) a limited partnership dissolved, notice of which was lodged with the Registrar of Limited Partnerships under section 19(2) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (f) VCC: winding up 2 years, struck off 6 years.
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(f)(i) a VCC dissolved following its winding up under Part 11 of the VCC Act` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(f)(ii) a VCC dissolved following its name being struck off the register under section 344 or 344A as applied by section 130B of the VCC Act` (Date 1 1 2021) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the Minister's consent; a name that is not identical; a registration before 3 January 2016.
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `s 378(2)(a)(i) a company dissolved following its winding up under Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) FALSE `s 378(2)(a)(i) a company dissolved following its winding up under Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 2 1 2016) TRUE `s 378(2)(a)(i) a company dissolved following its winding up under Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` (Date 1 1 2016) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "on or after 3 January 2016": the day itself counts.
#ASSERT `s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` FALSE (Date 3 1 2016) TRUE `s 378(2)(a)(i) a company dissolved following its winding up under Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` (Date 1 1 2016) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Section 378(3): names the Registrar may register despite subsection (1)`

-- Arguments: the day of the registration; the name is identical to the name of the earlier holder; the earlier holder; the day of the cessation or of the striking off.
-- (a)(i) 3 months after cessation on 1 January 2026 end on 1 April 2026.
#ASSERT `s 378(3) the Registrar may register the foreign company under the name` (Date 2 4 2026) TRUE `s 378(3)(a)(i) a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11, in respect of which notice was lodged under section 377(1) that it has ceased to have a place of business or to carry on business in Singapore` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(3) the Registrar may register the foreign company under the name` (Date 1 4 2026) TRUE `s 378(3)(a)(i) a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11, in respect of which notice was lodged under section 377(1) that it has ceased to have a place of business or to carry on business in Singapore` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a)(ii) 6 years after the striking off on 1 January 2020 end on 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `s 378(3) the Registrar may register the foreign company under the name` (Date 2 1 2026) TRUE `s 378(3)(a)(ii) a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11, the name of which was struck off the register under section 377(8), (9) or (10)` (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(3) the Registrar may register the foreign company under the name` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE `s 378(3)(a)(ii) a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11, the name of which was struck off the register under section 377(8), (9) or (10)` (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) a limited partnership, one year after the cessation on 1 January 2025.
#ASSERT `s 378(3) the Registrar may register the foreign company under the name` (Date 2 1 2026) TRUE `s 378(3)(b) a limited partnership in respect of which notice was lodged under section 19(1) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 that it ceased to carry on business in Singapore` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(3) the Registrar may register the foreign company under the name` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE `s 378(3)(b) a limited partnership in respect of which notice was lodged under section 19(1) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 that it ceased to carry on business in Singapore` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- before 3 January 2016, or a name that is not identical: the subsection speaks of neither.
#ASSERT `s 378(3) the Registrar may register the foreign company under the name` (Date 2 1 2016) TRUE `s 378(3)(b) a limited partnership in respect of which notice was lodged under section 19(1) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 that it ceased to carry on business in Singapore` (Date 1 1 2010) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 378(3) the Registrar may register the foreign company under the name` (Date 2 1 2026) FALSE `s 378(3)(b) a limited partnership in respect of which notice was lodged under section 19(1) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 that it ceased to carry on business in Singapore` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 378(4): the names a foreign company may use`

-- Arguments: this Division applies to the foreign company; the name is the registered name; the company is registered under the Business Names Registration Act 2014; the name is a business name registered under section 8 of that Act.
#ASSERT `s 378(4) the foreign company is barred from using the name in Singapore` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 378(4) the foreign company is barred from using the name in Singapore` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 378(4) the foreign company is barred from using the name in Singapore` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) needs both: registered under that Act, and the name a business name registered under section 8.
#ASSERT `s 378(4) the foreign company is barred from using the name in Singapore` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(4) the foreign company is barred from using the name in Singapore` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "No foreign company to which this Division applies": the bar names the companies it reaches.
#ASSERT `s 378(4) the foreign company is barred from using the name in Singapore` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 378(5) and (6): a direction to change a name`

-- (5) Arguments: the Registrar is satisfied of ground (a) (a name not permitted under (1)(a), (b) or (d)); ground (b) (a name not permitted under (2) until the period expires); ground (c) (a name permitted under (3) only after the period).
#ASSERT `s 378(5) the Registrar may direct the foreign company to change its name` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(5) the Registrar may direct the foreign company to change its name` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(5) the Registrar may direct the foreign company to change its name` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a "may" gated by "where": with no ground made out, the text's own gate says no (split site (ii)).
#ASSERT `s 378(5) the Registrar may direct the foreign company to change its name` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Arguments: the Registrar has directed the company to change its name; the Minister has annulled the direction.
#ASSERT `s 378(5) the foreign company must comply with the direction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(5) the foreign company must comply with the direction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 378(5) the foreign company must comply with the direction` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Arguments: the day of the direction; the day the company complied; the Registrar allowed a longer period; the last day of the longer period. Direction on 1 June 2026: 6 weeks (42 days) end on 13 July 2026.
#ASSERT `s 378(5) the foreign company complied with the direction within the time allowed` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 13 7 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(5) the foreign company complied with the direction within the time allowed` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 14 7 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 378(5) the foreign company complied with the direction within the time allowed` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 14 7 2026) TRUE (Date 31 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(5) the foreign company complied with the direction within the time allowed` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE (Date 31 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 378(5) the foreign company complied with the direction within the time allowed` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 14 7 2026) FALSE (Date 31 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- the 6 weeks (42 days): changed on day 42 it is fulfilled; on day 43, or never, it is breached.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 378(5) the foreign company must change its name within 6 weeks after the date of the direction` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 378(5) change its name as the Registrar directs` AT 42
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 378(5) the foreign company must change its name within 6 weeks after the date of the direction` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 378(5) change its name as the Registrar directs` AT 43
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 378(5) the foreign company must change its name within 6 weeks after the date of the direction` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 43)

-- the longer period the Registrar allows: 60 days from the direction.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 378(5) the foreign company must change its name within the longer period the Registrar allows` "Overseas Co" 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 378(5) change its name as the Registrar directs` AT 60
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 378(5) the foreign company must change its name within the longer period the Registrar allows` "Overseas Co" 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 378(5) change its name as the Registrar directs` AT 61
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 378(5) the foreign company must change its name within the longer period the Registrar allows` "Overseas Co" 60 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 61)

-- (6) Arguments: the application is in writing; it asks for a direction under subsection (5) on a ground referred to in that subsection.
#ASSERT `s 378(6) the person may apply to the Registrar to give a direction to the foreign company` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(6) the person may apply to the Registrar to give a direction to the foreign company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 378(6) the person may apply to the Registrar to give a direction to the foreign company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 378(7) and (8)`

-- (7) Arguments: the role of the person; the foreign company fails to comply with subsection (4); the officer is in default; the person knowingly and wilfully authorised or permitted the default.
-- the company: "a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a default penalty"; no term of imprisonment is stated.
#ASSERT (`s 378(7) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: the foreign company` TRUE FALSE FALSE)'s `s 378(7) the offence applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 378(7) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: the foreign company` TRUE FALSE FALSE)'s `s 378(7) the maximum fine, in dollars` EQUALS JUST 2000
#ASSERT (`s 378(7) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: the foreign company` TRUE FALSE FALSE)'s `s 378(7) the maximum term of imprisonment, in months` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 378(7) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: the foreign company` TRUE FALSE FALSE)'s `s 378(7) a default penalty also applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 378(7) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: the foreign company` FALSE FALSE FALSE)'s `s 378(7) the offence applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- every officer "who is in default".
#ASSERT (`s 378(7) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: an officer of the foreign company` TRUE TRUE FALSE)'s `s 378(7) the offence applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 378(7) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: an officer of the foreign company` TRUE FALSE FALSE)'s `s 378(7) the offence applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a director is an officer (s 4(1) "officer": "a director of the corporation").
#ASSERT (`s 378(7) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person` TRUE TRUE FALSE)'s `s 378(7) the offence applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 378(7) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person` TRUE FALSE FALSE)'s `s 378(7) the offence applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- every authorised representative "who knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the default".
#ASSERT (`s 378(7) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: an authorised representative of the foreign company` TRUE FALSE TRUE)'s `s 378(7) the offence applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 378(7) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: an authorised representative of the foreign company` TRUE TRUE FALSE)'s `s 378(7) the offence applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 378(7) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: an authorised representative of the foreign company` TRUE FALSE TRUE)'s `s 378(7) the maximum fine, in dollars` EQUALS JUST 2000
-- anyone else is not named.
#ASSERT (`s 378(7) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: someone else` TRUE TRUE TRUE)'s `s 378(7) the offence applies` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (8)
#ASSERT `s 378(8) the name is a registered business name` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(8) the name is a registered business name` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 378(9) and (10): appeals to the Minister`

-- (9)(a) Arguments: the decision was made on or after 3 January 2016; the person is the foreign company aggrieved by the decision; the day of the decision; the day the appeal is made. Decision on 1 April 2026: the thirtieth day is 1 May 2026.
#ASSERT `s 378(9)(a) the foreign company may appeal to the Minister against the Registrar's decision under subsection (5)` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(9)(a) the foreign company may appeal to the Minister against the Registrar's decision under subsection (5)` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 2 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 378(9)(a) the foreign company may appeal to the Minister against the Registrar's decision under subsection (5)` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 378(9)(a) the foreign company may appeal to the Minister against the Registrar's decision under subsection (5)` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (9)(b) Arguments: the decision was made on or after 3 January 2016; the person is the applicant aggrieved by the refusal; the day the applicant was informed; the day the appeal is made.
#ASSERT `s 378(9)(b) the applicant may appeal to the Minister against the Registrar's refusal to give a direction under subsection (5)` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(9)(b) the applicant may appeal to the Minister against the Registrar's refusal to give a direction under subsection (5)` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 2 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 378(9)(b) the applicant may appeal to the Minister against the Registrar's refusal to give a direction under subsection (5)` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (10)
#ASSERT `s 378(10) the Minister must cause the direction to be published in the Gazette` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(10) the Minister must cause the direction to be published in the Gazette` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 378(11) to (17): reservation of a name`

-- (11) Arguments: the application is in the prescribed form; it sets out the name.
#ASSERT `s 378(11) the person may apply to the Registrar for the reservation of the name` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(11) the person may apply to the Registrar for the reservation of the name` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 378(11) the person may apply to the Registrar for the reservation of the name` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (12) a bar: "must not be registered ... unless the name has been reserved".
#ASSERT `s 378(12) the foreign company must not be registered by the name` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(12) the foreign company must not be registered by the name` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (13) Arguments: satisfied that the application is made in good faith; satisfied that the name is one in respect of which a foreign company may be registered. "only if".
#ASSERT `s 378(13) the Registrar may approve the application` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(13) the Registrar may approve the application` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 378(13) the Registrar may approve the application` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (14) Arguments: satisfied of an unlawful or prejudicial purpose; satisfied that registration would be contrary to the national security or interest.
#ASSERT `s 378(14) the Registrar must refuse to approve the application to reserve the name` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(14) the Registrar must refuse to approve the application to reserve the name` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(14) the Registrar must refuse to approve the application to reserve the name` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (15)
#ASSERT `s 378(15) the Registrar must reserve the proposed name` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(15) the Registrar must reserve the proposed name` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Arguments: approved; the day the applicant was notified of the approval; extended by a further 60 days on an application in good faith; refused; the day the applicant was notified of the refusal.
-- approved, notified on 1 June 2026: 60 days after end on 31 July 2026; with the further 60 days, on 29 September 2026.
#ASSERT `s 378(15) the last day of the reservation` TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 7 2026)
#ASSERT `s 378(15) the last day of the reservation` TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 9 2026)
-- refused: the reservation ends on the date of notice of the refusal.
#ASSERT `s 378(15) the last day of the reservation` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE TRUE (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 6 2026)
-- neither: the text names no end.
#ASSERT `s 378(15) the last day of the reservation` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (16) Arguments: the person is aggrieved by a decision refusing approval or refusing the extension; the day the person was informed; the day the appeal is made. Informed on 1 April 2026: the thirtieth day is 1 May 2026.
#ASSERT `s 378(16) the person may appeal to the Minister` TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 378(16) the person may appeal to the Minister` TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 2 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 378(16) the person may appeal to the Minister` FALSE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
